<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty> .
<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#hasTopConcept> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "In DeSMòS, it relates a concept scheme to the concepts that are its main hierarchical entry points. The original property has domain skos:ConceptScheme and range skos:Concept. In DeSMòS, the same property has domain skos:ConceptScheme and range skos:Concept."@en .
<http://iflastandards.info/ns/lrm/lrmoo/R17i_was_created_by> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Inversa di R17 created: in DeSMòS collega un'espressione testuale all'evento compositivo che l'ha prodotta. La proprietà originale ha come domain lrmoo:F2_Expression e come range lrmoo:F28_Expression_Creation. In DeSMòS la stessa proprietà ha come domain lrmoo:F2_Expression e come range lrmoo:F28_Expression_Creation."@it .
<https://w3id.org/desmos/isSemanticUnitConstrainedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://w3id.org/lso/intro/beta202506#INT15_IntertextualityInIntertextualityTheories> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "In DeSMòS, INT15 Intertextuality in Intertextuality Theories è utilizzata per rappresentare tipi di relazione derivati da teorie dell'intertestualità, tra cui l'ipertestualità nella classificazione di Gérard Genette."@it .
<https://w3id.org/lso/intro/beta202506#INT1_Passage> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/lso/intro/beta202506#> .
