<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#ConceptScheme> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
<https://w3id.org/desmos/hypertextuality> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Hypertextuality"@en .
<http://iflastandards.info/ns/lrm/lrmoo/R15i_is_fragment_of> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Inverse of R15 has fragment: in DeSMòS, it relates a peritextual declaration to the expression of which it is a fragment. The original property has domain crm:E90_Symbolic_Object and range lrmoo:F2_Expression. In DeSMòS, the same property has domain crm:E33_Linguistic_Object and range lrmoo:F2_Expression."@en .
<http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P67i_is_referred_to_by> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The preferred term for representing the concept."@en .
<https://w3id.org/lso/intro/beta202506#INT11_TypeOfInterrelation> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/desmos/constrainsFormalUnit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relates a formal constraint to the textual unit on which it operates. The property has domain desmos:FormalConstraint and range skos:Concept."@en .
<https://w3id.org/desmos/LiteraryConstraint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Procedura formale o semantica che interviene nel processo di generazione testuale (F28 Expression Creation). La sua presenza può essere documentata attraverso evidenze oggettive (TextualFeature) o dichiarazioni paratestuali (E33 Linguistic Object)."@it .
<https://w3id.org/desmos/FormalConstraintScheme> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#ConceptScheme> .
<https://w3id.org/desmos/VisualConstraint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/desmos/> .
<http://iflastandards.info/ns/lrm/lrmoo/F1_Work> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/desmos/finerThan> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relates a formal unit to a formal unit of coarser textual granularity (e.g., a letter with respect to a syllable or a word), exclusively within the FormalUnitScheme. The property has domain skos:Concept and range skos:Concept."@en .
<https://w3id.org/desmos/finerThan> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P130_shows_features_of> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "P130 shows features of"@en .
<http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E70_Thing> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "In DeSMòS, E70 Thing is referenced as the original domain and range of P130 shows features of. E28 Conceptual Object is declared as its direct subclass, abbreviating the official chain E28 Conceptual Object ⊑ E71 Human-Made Thing ⊑ E70 Thing (CIDOC CRM 7.1.3)."@en .
<http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P14_carried_out_by> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#closeMatch> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "close match"@en .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/hasVersion> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/desmos/SemanticConstraintScheme> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Concept scheme collecting semantic constraints, which intervene primarily on the signified of the text."@en .
<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "comment"@en .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
<https://w3id.org/lso/intro/beta202506#R19_hasType> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/lso/intro/beta202506#> .
<https://w3id.org/desmos/isRevealedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Inverse of revealsConstraint: this property relates a literary constraint to the textual feature that makes it identifiable. The property has domain desmos:LiteraryConstraint and range desmos:TextualFeature."@en .
<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "definition"@en .
<https://w3id.org/desmos/isConstraintUsedIn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "è costrizione usata in"@it .
<http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E39_Actor> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/desmos/> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "DeSMòS (Descriptive Semantic Model for Structured Texts) is an OWL 2 ontology for the formal representation of literary constraints as text-generative procedures, with particular reference to the Oulipian tradition. The model treats constraints as conceptual entities distinct from works and their bibliographic realisations, represented through LRMoo, and describes their use in expression creation events, distinguishing the procedure from both the creative process and the resulting text. Constrained rewriting is represented through derivation and intertextual relations between expressions, allowing the identification of the textual passages involved. The typological characterisation distinguishes formal and semantic constraints, with a specific category for visual constraints, and describes the constrained units, procedural operations, and origins through SKOS controlled vocabularies. The model also supports the documentation of constraint use through intratextual evidence and paratextual statements, whether peritextual or epitextual, distinguishing responsibility for such statements from responsibility for textual creation. Through the reuse of and alignment with CIDOC CRM, LRMoo, PROV-O, SKOS, INTRO, Dublin Core Terms, and Schema.org, DeSMòS supports the description, comparative analysis, and SPARQL querying of constrained writing practices across heterogeneous corpora."@en .
_:N8d32349f039c4883a38925ad3d548524 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:Nbfd327fa25fe44a896e28a82ce189994 .
<http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2i_is_type_of> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Inverse of P2 has type: in DeSMòS, it relates a literary or artistic form type to the expressions it classifies. The original property has domain crm:E55_Type and range crm:E1_CRM_Entity. In DeSMòS, the same property has domain crm:E55_Type and range lrmoo:F2_Expression."@en .
<http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P2_has_type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "In DeSMòS, it classifies an expression by its literary or artistic form (e.g., prose, poetry, visual poetry). The original property has domain crm:E1_CRM_Entity and range crm:E55_Type. In DeSMòS, the same property has domain lrmoo:F2_Expression and range crm:E55_Type."@en .
<http://iflastandards.info/ns/lrm/lrmoo/R76_is_derivative_of> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://iflastandards.info/ns/lrm/lrmoo/F2_Expression> .
<http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "In DeSMòS, E33 Linguistic Object è utilizzata per identificare passaggi paratestuali (epitestuali o peritestuali) nei quali l'autore o il curatore del volume dichiara l'utilizzo di una costrizione letteraria. Le proprietà che possono essere usate con questa classe sono crm:P129_is_about, crm:P3_has_note, crm:P67_refers_to e prov:wasAttributedTo."@it .
<https://w3id.org/desmos/usedConstraint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "ha usato costrizione"@it .
<http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/P129_is_about> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "P129 is about"@en .
<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "In DeSMòS, the class is used to define individual literary constraints and analytical categories within an organized knowledge system. The properties that can be used with this class are desmos:coarserThan, desmos:constrainsFormalUnit, desmos:constrainsSemanticUnit, desmos:constraintOrigin, desmos:finerThan, desmos:involvesOperation, skos:broader, skos:closeMatch, skos:exactMatch, skos:inScheme, skos:narrower and skos:related."@en .
<https://w3id.org/lso/intro/beta202506#R12_hasReferredToEntity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "In DeSMòS, it identifies the hypotextual entity of an intertextual relation: the whole expression or, when the relation can be localised, a specific passage of the hypotext. The original property has domain intro:INT3_Interrelation and range the union of lrmoo:F1_Work, crm:E73_Information_Object, intro:INT1_Passage, intro:INT2_ActualizationOfFeature and intro:INT6_Architext. In DeSMòS, the same property has domain intro:INT31_IntertextualRelation and range lrmoo:F2_Expression or intro:INT21_TextPassage."@en .
<https://w3id.org/desmos/revealsConstraint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Inverse of isRevealedBy: this property relates a textual feature to the literary constraint it makes identifiable. The property has domain desmos:TextualFeature and range desmos:LiteraryConstraint."@en .
<http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E7_Activity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "E7 Activity"@en .
_:N68e9e0231c5f411b8c29f0290c98a2a2 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <https://w3id.org/lso/intro/beta202506#INT6_Architext> .
<https://w3id.org/desmos/involvesOperation> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#inverseOf> <https://w3id.org/desmos/isOperationInvolvedIn> .
<http://iflastandards.info/ns/lrm/lrmoo/R3i_realises> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Inversa di R3 is realised in: in DeSMòS collega un'espressione testuale all'opera che realizza. La proprietà originale ha come domain lrmoo:F2_Expression e come range lrmoo:F1_Work. In DeSMòS la stessa proprietà ha come domain lrmoo:F2_Expression e come range lrmoo:F1_Work."@it .
